# xcquinox.alec.cluster -- rsync filter rules for the "summaries" pull profile.
#
# Loaded via `rsync --filter='. <abs path>/summaries.filter'`. Rules apply with
# the run dir (`run_<UTC>Z/`) as the transfer root, so leading `/` anchors a
# pattern to that root (NOT the filesystem root). See `man rsync` "FILTER RULES"
# and "INCLUDE/EXCLUDE PATTERN RULES".
#
# Contract: this filter MUST stay in sync with the artifact layout the harness
# writes (see xcquinox/alec/cluster/__main__.py cmd_submit, _train_task.py,
# _eval_one_spec.py, _pretrain.py). When the harness gains a new small artifact,
# add a `+ ` line here in the same commit. The end-to-end canary test in
# tests/test_cluster_sync.py drives rsync against a fixture tree and will fail
# loudly if this filter omits an artifact it lists or includes a *.eqx blob it
# is not supposed to.
#
# The NETWORK WEIGHTS this profile carries (2026-08-30). The profile used to
# skip every *.eqx; it now carries the four the enhancement-factor figures read
# -- the trained model.eqx / model_val_best.eqx per spec with their .class.json
# records, and the pretrained xnet.eqx / cnet.eqx per architecture with the
# val-best pair beside them. Those figures (notebooks/analysis/trained_fx_fc.py
# and pretrain_fx_fc.py) forward-evaluate the networks themselves, which no
# summary table can stand in for, and the model class the loaders check is
# stated only by the .class.json record. They are small: the 1259 model*.eqx
# checkpoints on disk here measure 11.8 KB to 129 KB (median 32 KB), so a
# 100-cell run adds a few MB to a profile budgeted at under 100 MB -- the bulk
# of a `--profile full` pull is the logs/ tree and the per-step snapshots, not
# these. What stays remote is set out at the bottom of this file.

# --- top-level metadata (small, always wanted) -----------------------------
+ /manifest.json
+ /resolved_config.yaml
+ /jobs.json
+ /attempts.json
# The run-level representative-subset ledger: names every cell's selected
# training points; the figures and the exclusion layer both key on it.
+ /subset_ledger.json
# The staged validation slice (cluster/inputs._stage_validation_slice): the
# identity record of the 47-name validation set. The figures' validation
# column hard-requires it -- a pull without it silently rendered a DIFFERENT
# slice than the training's own.
+ /validation/
+ /validation/***

# --- shard scratch: excluded BEFORE the eval_holdout*/ includes below ------
# The parallel eval's worker shard payloads (names_t*_s*.json /
# shard_t*_s*.json). Already merged into per_molecule/per_reaction at eval
# time; measured ~60 percent of a summaries pull's bytes with no analysis
# use. First-match wins in rsync filters, so this line must stay ABOVE the
# `+ .../eval_holdout*/***` rules.
- /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout*/_shards/

# --- per-spec eval / training summaries ------------------------------------
# rsync needs `+ <dir>/` rules to descend into each level; the final `- *`
# below would otherwise prune the whole subtree.
+ /checkpoints/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_df.csv
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/failure.json
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/losses.npy
# aux_log.pkl (per-step, per-group, per-channel loss values) + train_metadata
# (config + final_loss) are the FIRST things needed to triage a NaN/divergent
# run -- small (~90 KB/spec), so pull them in `summaries` rather than forcing a
# multi-GB `--profile full`. (2026-06: a polarized-correlation NaN was diagnosed
# from aux_log.pkl, which the summaries profile had been dropping.)
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/aux_log.pkl
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/train_metadata.json
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval/per_molecule.json
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval/skipped.json
# Held-out (BH76 + W4-11) reaction-energy eval -- THE "beats PBE?" headline:
# eval_holdout/test_set.csv (mae_nn vs mae_pbe vs delta), per_reaction.json,
# per_molecule.json, and failure.json. This dir holds ONLY small text
# (CSV/JSON, no *.eqx), so `***` pulls the whole subtree present + future.
# (2026-06: the summaries profile had been dropping eval_holdout/ entirely, so
# the headline metric never reached a default pull -- guarded by the canary.)
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout/***
# Best-loss-checkpoint held-out eval (2026-06): a SECOND eval pass over the same
# pool using model_best.eqx instead of the final-step model.eqx, written to a
# sibling eval_holdout_best/ (same small CSV/JSON artifacts, no *.eqx). Doubles
# the figure data return; pulled by default like its eval_holdout/ sibling.
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_best/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_best/***
# Validation-best-checkpoint held-out eval (2026-06): a THIRD eval pass over the
# same pool using model_val_best.eqx (the held-out-VALIDATION-best weights). This
# is the checkpoint the figures now plot as "val-best" -- unlike model_best.eqx
# (min TRAINING loss, which selects the most-overfit step) it does not collapse on
# overfit-prone archs. Same small CSV/JSON, no *.eqx; pulled by default like its
# eval_holdout/ siblings so the default figures-only pull has the data.
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_val_best/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_val_best/***
# Cold-start trajectory-diagnostic channel (2026-08-14): a FOURTH eval pass on
# the FINAL checkpoint with the shared cold-start override (minao seed, 25
# cycles) -- the per-cycle scf_energy_residual_<i> columns + eval_metadata.json
# provenance stamp live here. Same small CSV/JSON artifacts, no *.eqx.
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_coldstart/
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/eval_holdout_coldstart/***

# --- trained network weights (2026-08-30) ----------------------------------
# The final-step and validation-best checkpoints, each with the model-class
# record beside it. The enhancement-factor figures (trained_fx_fc.py) build the
# skeleton from resolved_config.yaml and forward-evaluate these weights, and
# the loaders refuse an anchored or `dfs` checkpoint that arrives without its
# record (checkpoint_class.require_matching_class), so the .eqx and the
# .class.json must travel together or neither is usable.
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/model.eqx
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/model.eqx.class.json
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/model_val_best.eqx
+ /checkpoints/spec_*/model_val_best.eqx.class.json
# model_best.eqx (minimum TRAINING loss) is deliberately NOT here: it selects
# the most-overfit step on the overfit-prone archs and no figure reads it, so
# it stays remote to keep the default pull lean. Its held-out EVAL
# (eval_holdout_best/) still comes, as above. resume_*.eqx (the in-flight
# resume set, opt_state included) is mid-run state with no analysis use.

# --- pretrain metadata + loss curves (small, useful for diagnostics) -------
+ /pretrain/
+ /pretrain/*/
+ /pretrain/*/pretrain_metadata.json
# The per-arch fidelity certificate (fidelity.CERTIFICATE_FILENAME): the figure
# suite refuses to render an arch whose pulled run has no readable certificate,
# so the default pull must carry it (small JSON beside the metadata).
+ /pretrain/*/fidelity_certificate.json
+ /pretrain/*/losses_*.npy
# The pretrained networks themselves (2026-08-30), read by pretrain_fx_fc.py
# and by any local rebuild of a certified model: the final pair at the top
# level, the validated pair in the per-network subdirs pretrain.py writes
# (<arch>/xnet/xnet_val_best.eqx, <arch>/cnet/cnet_val_best.eqx), and any
# .class.json record standing beside one. 1.7 to 16 KB each. The periodic
# `xc.eqx.<step>` trajectory snapshots in those same subdirs are NOT included
# -- one per serialize interval per network, of no analysis use.
+ /pretrain/*/xnet.eqx
+ /pretrain/*/cnet.eqx
+ /pretrain/*/*.eqx.class.json
+ /pretrain/*/xnet/
+ /pretrain/*/xnet/xnet_val_best.eqx
+ /pretrain/*/xnet/xnet_val_best.eqx.class.json
+ /pretrain/*/cnet/
+ /pretrain/*/cnet/cnet_val_best.eqx
+ /pretrain/*/cnet/cnet_val_best.eqx.class.json

# --- drop everything else -------------------------------------------------
# This includes: /logs/, /scripts/, /specs/, every *.eqx NOT named above
# (model_best.eqx, the resume_*.eqx set, the pretrain `xc.eqx.<step>`
# snapshots, and any stray .eqx elsewhere in the tree), every per-spec
# *.gen<N> archived artifact, and any future top-level dir the harness gains
# (must be opted in explicitly above).
- *
